,$ then $b=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110318 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5204a10c-ec1e-5276-95f2-0842b4c1bdf5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110318 #edb/ref 1074 "If we substitute ${\\color{blue}{b}}={\\color{blue}{4}}$ into the given equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2b & =8 \\\\ 2\\cdot 4 & =8 \\\\ 8 & =8\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $b=4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110319 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13061" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110319 #edb/ref 1071 "If  $\\dfrac{15}{c} = 5,$ then $c=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110319 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e2be2f3b-d507-5447-9ed0-d164374a8b4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110319 #edb/ref 1074 "If we substitute ${\\color{blue}{c}}={\\color{blue}{3}}$ into the given equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{15}{c} & =5 \\\\ \\frac{15}{3} & =5 \\\\ 5 & =5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $c = \\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110737 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110737 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110737 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110737 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186479829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110737 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186479864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110737 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Linear Equations Involving Addition" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110737 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110737 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "a7f85a2c-76f2-5c56-b6a0-3a0cc95150b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110738 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111231 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110738 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110738 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186479839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110738 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186479847 #edb/ref 175